WEBVTT

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.680
What is the meaning of this?!

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.680
Yuzu's gotten pretty good at her work.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.890
I'm telling you to take a break.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.590
You're a workaholic as it is.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.500
That's for me to decide!

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.600
I'm in perfect health. I'm fine!

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.860
Who's going to take my place, anyway?

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.320
<i>That </i>is not for you to decide.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.640
Listen, you're going to take tomorrow off.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.490
I know how you feel, Satsuki,

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:35.070
but you aren't going to get out of Konohanatei 
just because you work especially hard.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.470
Um...

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.490
I-Is something wrong with Satsuki-chan?

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:25.040
<b>Konohana Kitan</b>

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:30.040
<b>Episode 2
Spring Journey</b>

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.250
<i>You aren't going to get out of Konohanatei 
just because you work especially hard.</i>

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.170
<i>I know that.</i>

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:54.840
<i>But the more time I waste, 
the further I get set apart from her.</i>

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.580
What the hell?!

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:03.550
It's a cherry blossom bath.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.530
I heard we're draining this bath tomorrow.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:09.960
I hope you enjoy it.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.940
I've never had sake in an outdoor bath before.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.060
Although Kiri does it all the time.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.970
Do you not like sake?

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.940
I don't drink at night.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:28.850
I usually have to make plans 
and prepare for the next day.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:31.190
You can get a good night's sleep today, then.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.740
<i>Right...</i>

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:38.660
<i>I don't need to think about anything tonight.</i>

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:44.750
It'll be a full moon soon.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.750
<i>When did I stop looking up at the sky?</i>

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:55.460
The world moves forward, 
no matter what we do.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:03.480
Blink or look down at your feet, 
and the scenery changes in a heartbeat.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:08.680
It would be a shame not to notice it.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.880
<i>A shame, huh?</i>

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:21.770
<i>This, too, is a remnant of the spring that 
had passed by while I was looking down.</i>

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.630
Do you want to be putting in all of this work?

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.190
I'm sure you're tired, too.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.410
I'm fine.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.160
I've got tomorrow off, too.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.570
Screw this. Join me!

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:48.940
O-Okay.

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.340
<i>Is she drunk?</i>

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.550
You said you have tomorrow off, right?

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.380
Perfect.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:57.600
Come with me.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.060
Huh? Where?

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.510
You haven't hung out in town yet, have you?

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.020
I'll show you around.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.770
I'll treat you to something nice in return 
for the cherry blossoms and sake.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.100
You don't need to.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:13.050
Besides, um, I don't have anything to wear.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.940
I'll lend you a kimono.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.170
See you there.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.910
<i>My first time going out!</i>

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.080
Unbelievable!

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:28.570
Are you really going to go out with 
that bedhead, Satsuki-neesama?

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.700
It's not like I have work today.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:31.690
Absolutely not.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.190
Go fix it immediately.

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:35.050
And your obi's the wrong color, Yuzu-chan!

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.930
I'll lend you one. Come with me.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:42.110
I can't stand it when girls 
are indifferent about fashion.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.480
What?

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:51.100
Oh, I, um... I've never seen you 
raise your voice before, Ren-chan.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:59.030
Pardon me. A lady must be graceful, 
even if her house is on fire.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:01.290
<i>She's cute, </i>and<i> she's amusing!</i>

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.070
Huh? Satsuki, there's a hole in your sock.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.550
Oh, I guess it's oka—

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:06.440
It's not okay!

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:07.820
Change it!

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:11.860
<i>I've never seen Satsuki-chan 
getting scolded.</i>

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:14.770
Ren, what time were the guests coming today?

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:16.090
<i>She still has all kinds of expressions 
that I've never seen before.</i>

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.730
Two parties at six.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:17.630
Righto.

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:19.590
Satsuki-neesama is attractive.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:21.220
I wish she would be more mindful.

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:25.420
She'll have to worry about her appearance 
even more if she becomes a priestess.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:27.400
Huh?

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.300
What? You haven't heard?

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:35.030
Satsuki-neesama is going to leave 
Konohanatei to become a priestess.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.940
<i>Satsuki-chan is...</i>

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.470
<i>leaving Konohanatei?</i>

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:44.760
What a swell day for an outing.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.710
What? You're being weird.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:51.610
I never thought <i>you</i> would 
invite Yuzu on a date.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.220
I'm just showing her around town 
because I suddenly have nothing to do,

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.930
thanks to a certain someone.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.630
Kiri! Kiri!

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.010
Yes, Okami?

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:01.860
We're going to have two 
additional banquet guests.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.570
Okay, I'll inform the kitchen.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:05.850
Thanks.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:08.280
Hey, are you sure...

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.330
It's fine! We don't have too many 
people staying tonight.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.520
Just go!

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:21.650
We left late because Ren held us up.

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:24.040
You look so pretty, though, Satsuki-chan.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:27.670
<i>There she goes with her shamelessly 
embarrassing comments again.</i>

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.930
Satsuki-chan, look at that!

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:30.960
How cute!

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:33.640
Maneki-nekos!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.940
There are so many of them!

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:37.050
We have all kinds of faces.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.140
Come take a look.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:42.480
The one with its right paw 
up brings good fortune,

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:42.840
You like cats?

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.190
and the one with its left 
paw up brings in customers.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:43.600
Yes!

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:44.580
Really?

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.330
Cats aren't that tasty, though.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:52.070
<b>Salt</b>

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:52.060
Shoo! Shoo!

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.240
There are more shops over there.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.520
Want to check them out?

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:51.340
Okay.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.510
You're having mitarashi 
dango, huh, Satsuki-chan?

00:07:58.510 --> 00:07:59.620
They look good.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.750
May I have a bite?

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:03.280
Okay.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:09.370
<i>Girls do like this kind of thing.</i>

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:10.940
You can have a bite of this, too.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.210
O-Okay...

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.170
Here you go.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:16.890
Here.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:21.440
See?

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:24.600
The shiratama is all jiggly and tasty.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.480
<i>N-No one's watching, right?</i>

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.270
It's such a big city.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:38.000
I used to live at a temple in the 
mountains, so I was shocked at first.

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:41.420
You seem comfortable around people, though.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.760
The temple had a lot of visitors.

00:08:44.110 --> 00:08:47.250
We had a lot of human visitors, too.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:48.670
<i>I see.</i>

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:52.770
<i>No wonder she tends to have 
a lot of human knowledge.</i>

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.460
There are humans in this 
town occasionally, too.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:58.680
Really?

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:01.640
It's a post town for travelers.

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:04.600
You can expect to see 
just about anyone here.

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:07.560
It's beautiful.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:14.800
It's exciting when you think that everyone 
who passes by has their own secrets.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:15.990
Is it?

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:20.210
Thank you very much 
for inviting me out today.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:26.280
As long as you're having fun, I guess.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:27.020
Yep.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.870
<i>I just had time to spare.</i>

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.540
<i>I never did anything to be thanked for.</i>

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.180
<i>That would be easy enough to say.</i>

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:39.550
<b>Dango</b>

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:39.130
<i>So why can't I say that to her?</i>

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.520
<i>Don't go getting weird ideas!</i>

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.040
<i>If this were Kiri, I'd totally say it.</i>

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.020
<i>The tsundere look doesn't suit you.</i>

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:46.800
<i>This girl throws me off, somehow.</i>

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:48.490
Long time no see, Tome-san.

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:51.070
Have the cherry blossoms 
bloomed at the shrine yet?

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:52.430
About that...

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:56.940
The cherry blossom season's over, 
and the tree hasn't grown a single bud.

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:59.170
I suppose it's just too old now.

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:01.090
That's a shame.

00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:04.950
You'll never see such a fine 
sacred tree anywhere else.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.570
So, where should we go next?

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.530
I want to see the shrine.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:11.760
The shrine?

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:17.070
There's nothing interesting to see there.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:21.340
I, um... just want to pay 
my respects to the god.

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:24.510
I'm curious about the cherry
 blossom tree, too... and...

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:29.150
I want to see where you'll be working.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:34.070
Where I'll what?

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:36.860
Ren told you, didn't she?!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.190
That blabbermouth!

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.230
I-It's not her fault!

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:43.710
I probably made a mistake.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:48.840
Besides, I think you'd 
make a great priestess.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.290
Don't go picturing that!

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:53.160
Where are you going?

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.010
The washroom.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:56.660
Sorry.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.520
<i>D-Did I say something to upset her?</i>

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.700
<i>I have to be careful.</i>

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.730
Listen. Stay there so you don't get lost.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.300
<i>She still worries about me, even now.</i>

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:12.240
<i>She's so kind.</i>

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:22.110
Are you okay?

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:24.500
Thank you.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.820
I got separated from my sister.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.740
I've been looking for her for five days now.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:31.800
Five days?

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:35.640
I still have work to do.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.390
What a predicament...

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:43.100
Um...

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:47.060
I-If it's okay, I'd like to help you look for her.

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:49.580
I'd be grateful.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:53.480
<i>I'm sorry, Satsuki-chan. 
I'll be right back...</i>

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.190
Guess I should head back now.

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:04.900
Hey! You there, girl.

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:06.570
<i>That was bad.</i>

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.990
<i>No matter how irritated I was,</i>

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:09.760
I'm talking to you.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:12.870
<i>it was childish of me to show such 
attitude to a younger newcomer.</i>

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.900
I'm lost. Show me where to go.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:18.300
<i>Knowing Yuzu, I'm sure she'll 
pretend she's forgotten about it.</i>

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:19.150
Don't act like you don't hear me.

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:20.890
Rats, I couldn't get away.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:24.040
You don't get to call me "girl," child.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:25.120
Get lost.

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:25.850
How dare you!

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:28.360
Mistreat me, and I'll cry.

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:30.080
I'll roll around and wail.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.170
Do you want that?

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:34.750
You'd be the subject of ridicule 
if I followed you around rolling.

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:35.930
What kind of threat is that?

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:39.500
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.770
Fine, fine.

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:44.610
I'm glad you understand.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.900
<i>Sorry, Yuzu. I'll buy 
you a maneki-neko later.</i>

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:50.770
So, where do I need to take you?

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.590
Find my sister for me.

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:53.750
So you're just lost.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:54.880
I'm not lost!

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:58.810
I went off to have fun when my sister 
wasn't looking, and now I can't get home.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.020
That's even worse.

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:02.600
Just go away and live by yourself.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.310
How rude.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:11.750
I-I'm tired of my sister mocking me 
just because I'm younger than her.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:14.780
I'm not a child anymore.

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:20.950
Well, older sisters are pretty selfish.

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:23.260
What? You have an older sister, too?

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:24.040
<i>Shoot!</i>

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:25.220
We'll get along well.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:26.660
We don't need to!

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.910
I haven't seen anyone like that.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:30.880
I see.

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:32.730
Thank you.

00:13:33.090 --> 00:13:36.000
Sorry, I don't know the area very well.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.080
That's all right.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.970
Sorry to trouble you.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.840
Where are you traveling to?

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:44.980
To the north.

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:50.900
We travel from the southernmost 
point, slowly northward.

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:53.800
All of the others have already gone ahead.

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:56.280
My sister and I fell behind.

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:59.930
What? You need to catch 
up to them soon, then!

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:01.730
Not to worry.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:06.340
This journey has been undertaken 
countless times through the years.

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:12.510
Panic as I may, I can never 
outrun the passing of time.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.420
That's a beautiful thought.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:19.180
<i>Satsuki-neesama is going 
to become a priestess.</i>

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:21.740
<i>I was actually sad.</i>

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:24.350
<i>But we aren't parting for life.</i>

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:30.000
<i>There's still a lot that I don't know 
about this city, about Konohanatei,</i>

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.700
<i>and about my friends.</i>

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:38.060
<i>But I want to spend more time 
getting to like them even more.</i>

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:42.130
Hey, we'll be good friends, don't you think?

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:44.000
Damn it, shut up!

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.210
What is your older sister like?

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:47.740
Is she selfish?

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:48.830
<i>Really</i> selfish.

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:50.880
She's self-centered and tactless and...

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:53.270
great at everything.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.090
I have no interest in becoming a priestess.

00:14:58.090 --> 00:14:59.940
Let Satsuki have the job.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:02.600
Her dream is to serve the gods.

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:06.580
She's seriously an awful person.

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:10.990
My sister doesn't think about others, 
but she's not an awful person.

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:13.340
<i>Damn it, I want to smack her!</i>

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:15.300
I like you.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:16.930
Why don't you join me?

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:17.750
No, thank you!

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:18.750
What?

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.020
It's noble work, serving the gods.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:27.160
And not just a guardian deity 
to a small town like this one.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.860
We serve the gods of Takamagahara.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:33.450
It's a noble task, ensuring 
the well-being of Nakatsukuni.

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:37.400
You can give your sister 
a run for her money.

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:41.120
We'll send Hiiragi to serve at Konohanatei.

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:47.210
But dear, everyone expects 
Hiiragi to become a priestess.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:48.740
Indeed.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:51.860
Then let's send Satsuki instead.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:56.970
Gotcha.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:06.270
What the?!

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.330
Where did this gust come from?

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:09.480
A tornado?

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:13.650
I found her.

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:16.130
She's near the great cherry blossom tree.

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:21.070
If I can make the cherry blossoms bloom, 
my sister will think differently of me.

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:24.870
I can't do it by myself, 
but I have a friend with me now!

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:26.920
Wait! A friend?

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:29.960
You aren't going to use me 
to fertilize the tree, are you?

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.800
S-Someone...

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.910
Let's make flowers bloom on the dead tree!

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:48.130
The cherry blossom...

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.080
The great cherry blossom tree has flowered!

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:51.970
This calls for a banquet!

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:53.340
Time for a festival!

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:43.510
I found you, Satsuki-chan.

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:48.090
I was worried you might 
be stuck in the toilet.

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:51.180
<i>See? There you go.</i>

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:55.840
<i>You act like nothing happened.</i>

00:18:57.830 --> 00:18:59.110
Are you all right?

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.560
Y-Yes...

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:02.720
You shouldn't have tugged 
me without warning.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:03.410
Oh, my!

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:06.700
A priestess?

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:07.650
Ayame.

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:09.380
Satsuki-san.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:12.250
It's not often that I get to see you here.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.670
No, er, I...

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.800
Come, I'll find you a seat.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.080
W-Wait, Ayame!

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:21.430
Not to worry. I'll have a spot
for your companion, too.

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:36.270
What's the matter?

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:39.540
Someone was looking for her sister.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:40.470
Her sister?

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:44.200
Sh-She... seemed like she really needed help.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.200
I know you told me not to move, but...

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:47.830
Sorry.

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:51.540
No, well, I'm in no position to complain.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.170
It's fine.

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:56.450
She found her.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.850
The one in the middle.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:05.620
Do you see the silver-haired priestess?

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:09.050
That's my older sister.

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:13.960
I came to Konohanatei in her place.

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:17.370
I wasn't the one chosen 
to become a priestess.

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:23.690
It's not that I've given up.

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:27.310
Once I'm free to resign, I'm going 
to aim to become a priestess again.

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:34.360
I'm self-conscious about this, 
so don't tell anyone.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:39.840
<i>She's so kind.</i>

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:46.380
<i>She's kind, and clumsy, and doesn't want 
to talk to people about herself.</i>

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:48.820
<i>And yet she revealed her secret to me.</i>

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:03.710
<i>I never knew it could make me 
so happy to touch someone's heart.</i>

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:07.270
Wh-What?

00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:08.570
What happened to you?

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:20.120
I'm so glad I came to Konohanatei 
and met everybody, especially you.

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:26.630
Let's go.

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:32.670
There's a banquet at the main hall.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:34.930
Let's get back to work.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:41.400
Okay.

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:53.170
<i>Ever northward they travel, leaving 
behind the footsteps of the bloom.</i>

00:21:54.340 --> 00:21:55.730
<i>Let's go home.</i>

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:59.410
<i>Back to our Konohanatei.</i>

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Next Episode
Waiting Lovesick</b>
